nrsc5-studio (0.3.10-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Antenna selector in the Tuner panel for multi-input SDRplay RSPs
    (RSPduo, RSPdx). Single-input devices unaffected (dropdown only
    renders when the live SDR reports more than one antenna). The
    chosen antenna persists into config.toml under [sdr] antenna.
  * Manual gain slider now hot-applies mid-stream instead of
    requiring a restart. Routes through the same apply_agc_action
    path the closed-loop AGC uses, so the slider drag feels
    identical to AGC probing.
  * No DSP / decoder / packaging-script behavior change versus
    0.3.9 — the new code is UI wiring on top of existing trait
    methods.

 -- LTCAshraven <ltcashraven@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 27 May 2026 14:00:00 +0000

nrsc5-studio (0.3.9-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Opus 96 kbps session recording with per-subchannel files, Vorbis
    tags (title/artist/station), and time-based rotation.
  * Recordings now default to a portable folder next to the
    executable instead of ~/Documents/nrsc5-studio/recordings/.
  * Theme-aware accent color: light mode now passes WCAG-AA contrast
    (RGB 28,100,210 ~5.5:1 on white) without darkening the dark-mode
    accent.
  * Fixed: constellation scope no longer loses lock when switching
    subchannels (was inferring sync state from transient status text;
    now reads the authoritative sync bool).
  * Updated cargo-deb / cargo-generate-rpm metadata to install the
    .desktop launcher, AppStream metainfo, manpage, and hicolor
    icons (16/32/48/64/128/256px) into standard XDG paths.

 -- LTCAshraven <ltcashraven@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 26 May 2026 14:00:00 +0000

nrsc5-studio (0.3.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Linux packaging debut. .deb and .rpm now built from the same Rust
    source tree as the Windows portable zip. No DSP/SDR behavior
    change versus 0.3.6 — packaging metadata, install scripts,
    AppStream metainfo, .desktop launcher, hicolor icons, manpage,
    and a first-launch missing-helper dialog.
  * End-user .deb builds are produced by cargo-deb against
    [package.metadata.deb] in Cargo.toml (see packaging/debian/README.md).

 -- LTCAshraven <LTCAshraven@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 24 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

